<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28230" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοχμή</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόχμη</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέχομαι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>space
				contained in a hand's breadth,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				350
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				318
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
				571
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Scyl.
				112
			</span></i>: expld. as, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παλαιστή</span>
			, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
			</span></i> ad loc.; but also as, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπιθαμή</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i> s. h. v.; <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i> give both senses. (On the accent, v.
			<i><span class="en">
				Ael.Dion.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				136
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				2.157
			</span></i>.)</div>
